  "id": "thecherrypit",
  "neon": "#ff2e8e",
  "note": "A club on the swanky west strip, and low enough that a tower trick would look silly on it. The form is a CROSS instead: a square main floor with a second one turned thirty degrees through it at the same height, so the plan has eight corners and the roofline steps round itself, under a faceted drum. It is the same coincident-box idea as chromeclinic.json used sideways — there for a chamfer, here deliberately coarse enough to read as two buildings jammed together, which is what the room description has always said the place is. RENDER_TUNE.legacyArms puts the strip arm back.",
